2️⃣ Shell — the user interface 🖥️

=============================================
What the shell is
=============================================
The shell is a command interpreter.

It:

Takes commands from the user
Interprets them
Asks the kernel to execute them

👉 Shell ≠ Kernel

=============================================
Common shells
=============================================

bash (most common)
sh
zsh
fish

Example flow
ls -l


What happens:
Shell reads the command
Shell finds /bin/ls
Shell asks kernel to execute it
Kernel runs it and returns output

=============================================
Why shell matters
=============================================
Automation (scripts)
System administration
DevOps / SRE work


Final:

The shell is a command-line interface that allows users to interact with the Linux kernel by executing commands and scripts.
